WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.320
Every   useful   voice  

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.680
AI   project   starts  

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.320
with   a   business  

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.400
question.   In   HarborVoice,  

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.260
that   question   is  

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.640
simple:   where   is  

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.080
my   shipment?   The  

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:09.880
terminal   and   its  

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.981
records   are   fictional.  

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.840
The   engineering   boundaries  

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.520
are   real.   Nora  

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.080
asks   for   an  

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.680
exact   reference,   then  

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.500
calls   the   shipment  

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.900
lookup   tool.   A  

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.420
recorded   customs   hold  

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.360
stays   a   customs  

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.880
hold.   An   estimated  

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.040
arrival   stays   an  

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.580
estimate.   The   knowledge  

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.920
base   explains   published  

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.360
procedures,   while   tool  

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.400
results   provide   the  

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.980
shipment   facts.   If  

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.200
a   lookup   fails,  

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.180
Nora   must   say  

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.260
so.   If   the  

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.540
customer   needs   help,  

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.560
the   assistant   prepares  

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.300
a   request   for  

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.080
human   review.   Pending  

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.000
review   does   not  

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.720
mean   approved,   transferred  

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.160
or   released.   The  

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.360
public   visitor   agent  

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.280
has   a   separate,  

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.520
read-only   tool   and  

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.420
a   bounded   trial  

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.160
window.   The   engineering  

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.680
workspace   adds   versioned  

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.020
scenarios,   provider   simulations  

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.160
and   explicit   failure  

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.020
cases.   These   results  

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.120
describe   the   tests  

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:57.701
that   were   run;  

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:58.720
they   do   not  

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.980
promise   perfect   future  

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.080
conversations.   Explore   the  

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.019
working   demonstration,   inspect  

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:04.879
the   source   and  

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:05.921
compare   the   evidence.  

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.260
HarborVoice   brings   voice,  

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.300
knowledge   and   human  

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.580
control   into   one  

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.860
transparent   workflow.
